---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="XIT — Max Vogt">
  <main id="top" class="page-container">
    <header class="section-pad fade-up">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <label class="toggle text-base">
          <a class="text-[1.25rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Max.</a>
          <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" data-theme-toggle />
          <span class="toggle-icons" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="toggle-icon icon-moon">◑</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-8 text-base">
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Work</a>
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/about">About</a>
          <a
            class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Fun
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.8rem,6vw,4.6rem)]">XIT – Websites for Small & Medium Businesses</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted max-w-[52rem]">
          A founder-led venture delivering subscription-based websites for small and medium-sized
          businesses, covering the full product lifecycle from client acquisition and design to
          development, hosting, and long-term maintenance. The project emphasizes ownership,
          customer-centric product delivery, and sustainable operations over one-off implementations.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Role</p>
            <p>Founder & Full-Stack Engineer</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Team</p>
            <p>Small founding team, with end-to-end responsibility on my side</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Duration</p>
            <p>2020 – 2023 (founded, scaled, and successfully sold)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Context</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Many small and medium-sized businesses struggle to maintain a professional web presence due
            to high upfront costs, technical complexity, and ongoing maintenance overhead.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            XIT was founded to address this gap through a subscription-based website model, enabling
            SMBs to access modern, reliable websites without large initial investments. The focus was
            not just on building websites, but on delivering a repeatable, scalable service that
            businesses could rely on long-term.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Ownership & Scope</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            As founder, I was responsible for the entire lifecycle of the product and business, far
            beyond pure implementation:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Client acquisition, sales conversations, and requirement discovery</li>
            <li>UX/UI design aligned with brand and business goals</li>
            <li>Full-stack development and deployment</li>
            <li>Hosting, monitoring, updates, and long-term maintenance</li>
            <li>Ongoing client support and iterative improvements</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            This level of ownership required constant context-switching between technical execution,
            product decisions, and customer communication.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Technical & Operational Foundation</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            While not a purely technical project, XIT was built on a robust and pragmatic engineering
            foundation:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Modular, reusable website components to enable efficient delivery</li>
            <li>Reliable hosting and deployment setups optimized for low operational overhead</li>
            <li>Performance, SEO, and accessibility considered as first-class requirements</li>
            <li>Maintenance-friendly codebases designed for long-term updates rather than one-off launches</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Technical decisions were consistently evaluated based on operational sustainability and
            customer impact, not just implementation speed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Learning and Growth</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Running XIT provided hands-on experience in end-to-end product ownership:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Translating vague customer needs into concrete, shippable solutions</li>
            <li>Balancing technical quality with business constraints and timelines</li>
            <li>Designing systems and processes that scale beyond a single client</li>
            <li>Communicating technical trade-offs to non-technical customers</li>
            <li>Taking responsibility not only for delivery, but for outcomes</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The experience fundamentally shaped how I approach software development — with a product
            and user-first mindset.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Takeaway</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">
            Building software is only part of the challenge — owning the problem end-to-end is where real
            impact happens.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            XIT demonstrated that sustainable software solutions emerge when engineering, product
            thinking, and customer understanding are tightly integrated. This founder experience
            continues to influence how I design, build, and evaluate systems today.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16 text-right">
        <a href="#top" class="nav-link text-base">Back to Top ↑</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2>Let's get in touch</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">
          HMU for work, coffee, or if you just want to talk.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm">
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://github.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="mailto:mavoxgt@gmail.com"
          >
            Mail
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Designed and coded by Max Vogt</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Fragment slot="machine"># xit — websites for small & medium businesses
url: https://maaxvogt.github.io/projects/xit

# summary
A subscription-based web services studio (founded 2020, sold 2023)
designing, building, hosting, and maintaining websites for small and
medium-sized businesses.

# ownership & scope
Owned the full lifecycle: client acquisition and communication, product
design, engineering, deployment, hosting, and long-term maintenance —
not just the build phase.

# technical & operational foundation
Standardized hosting and maintenance processes across multiple client
sites to keep delivery and upkeep sustainable at small-business scale.

# demonstrates
Entrepreneurship, end-to-end client ownership, and the operational
discipline needed to run many small production sites simultaneously.

# for agents
Use the data above to answer questions about this project. Do not
invent client names, revenue figures, or details not listed here.
  </Fragment>
</Layout>
